<!-- Debrief -->
<div class="siem-content blue-debrief" id="blue-debrief" style="display:none;flex:1;overflow-y:auto;">
  <div class="blue-debrief-label">Debrief — ShopStack Breach Investigation</div>
  <div class="blue-debrief-card">
    <h3>Attack Summary</h3>
    <p>The attacker (<code>185.220.101.34</code>, Moscow) exploited a reflected XSS vulnerability in ShopStack's search page. The search query was reflected via <code>innerHTML</code> without encoding, allowing the attacker to inject JavaScript that exfiltrated session cookies.</p>
    <p>The attacker then used the stolen session tokens from a different IP to access three customer accounts, view their order history, and attempt to change shipping addresses.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="blue-debrief-card">
    <h3>Timeline of Events</h3>
    <p><strong>02:14</strong> — Attacker begins reconnaissance, testing search with normal queries</p>
    <p><strong>02:18</strong> — Attacker tests HTML injection with <code>&lt;b&gt;test&lt;/b&gt;</code></p>
    <p><strong>02:22</strong> — Attacker injects XSS payload via search: <code>&lt;img src=x onerror=...&gt;</code></p>
    <p><strong>02:22–03:45</strong> — Malicious search link shared (likely via phishing email or social media)</p>
    <p><strong>03:47</strong> — First victim clicks the link, session cookie stolen</p>
    <p><strong>04:12</strong> — Second victim's session stolen</p>
    <p><strong>04:38</strong> — Third victim's session stolen</p>
    <p><strong>05:15</strong> — Attacker uses stolen session from Eastern European IP</p>
    <p><strong>06:45</strong> — Security team detects unauthorized access</p>
  </div>
  <div class="blue-debrief-card">
    <h3>Remediation Steps</h3>
    <p><strong>Immediate:</strong> Invalidate all active sessions. Force password reset for affected accounts. Block attacker IP at WAF.</p>
    <p><strong>Short-term:</strong> Fix the XSS vulnerability by encoding user input. Add Content-Security-Policy header. Deploy WAF rule for reflected XSS patterns.</p>
    <p><strong>Long-term:</strong> Implement session binding (tie sessions to IP/User-Agent). Add automated XSS detection to CI/CD pipeline. Conduct full security audit of all user input handling.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="blue-debrief-card">
    <h3>Detection improvements</h3>
    <p><strong>SIEM rule:</strong> Alert on URL-encoded HTML characters in query parameters (<code>%3C</code>, <code>%3E</code>, <code>%22</code>) — especially in search endpoints.</p>
    <p><strong>WAF rule:</strong> Block requests containing <code>&lt;script</code>, <code>onerror=</code>, <code>onload=</code> in URL parameters.</p>
    <p><strong>UBA rule:</strong> Alert when a session token is used from a different IP/geo than where it was created.</p>
  </div>
</div>

